/*!
\page page_strhicfhit StRHICfHit

\brief Reconstructed shower data from the RHICf dual-tower calorimeter.

\section rhicfhit_overview Overview

StRHICfHit stores the full reconstructed shower information for the
**RHICf very-forward calorimeter** (η > 6).  The detector has two towers (small: tower 0,
large: tower 1), each with 16 longitudinal GSO sampling plates and position-sensitive
GSO bars (20 bars for the small tower, 40 for the large).

The class stores energy deposits in plates and bars (always present) plus optional
dynamic arrays for shower depth parameters (L20, L90) and single/multi-shower fit
results.  Call \c initDataArray() before accessing the optional arrays.

**Detector**: RHICf very-forward calorimeter (η > 6)  
**Stage**: ADC → energy calibration → shower reconstruction

\section rhicfhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StRHICfHit
\endcode

Stored in \c StRHICfCollection.

\section rhicfhit_geometry Geometry

| Constant | Value | Meaning |
|----------|-------|---------|
| \c kRHICfNtower | 2 | Towers (0 = small, 1 = large) |
| \c kRHICfNplate | 16 | GSO sampling plates per tower |
| \c kRHICfNlayer | 4 | Bar readout layers |
| \c kRHICfNbarSmall | 20 | Bars in small tower |
| \c kRHICfNbarLarge | 40 | Bars in large tower |

\section rhicfhit_members Data Members

Always-present arrays (streamed):

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Float_t[2][16] | \c mPlateE | GSO plate energies [tower][plate] (GeV) |
| \c Float_t[4][2][20] | \c mGSOBarSmallE | Small-tower bar energies [layer][xy][bar] (GeV) |
| \c Float_t[4][2][40] | \c mGSOBarLargeE | Large-tower bar energies [layer][xy][bar] (GeV) |

Optional arrays (allocated by \c initDataArray()):

| Member | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c mL20 | Shower depth at 20% containment (X₀) per tower |
| \c mL90 | Shower depth at 90% containment (X₀) per tower |
| \c mSingleHitPos | Single-shower transverse position (mm) |
| \c mMultiHitPos | Multi-shower component positions (mm) |
| \c mMultiEnergySum | Multi-shower energy sums (GeV) |

\section rhicfhit_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c initDataArray() | Allocate optional TArray data |
| \c isSaveDataArray() | True if optional arrays are allocated |
| \c getPlateEnergy(tower, plate) | Sampling plate energy (GeV) |
| \c getGSOBarEnergy(tower, layer, xy, bar) | GSO bar energy (GeV) |
| \c getL20(tower), \c getL90(tower) | Shower depth parameters (X₀) |
| \c getSingleHitPos(tower, layer, xy) | Single-shower position (mm) |
| \c getMultiHitPos(tower, layer, xy, order) | Multi-shower component position (mm) |

\section rhicfhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StRHICfHit* hit = rhicfColl->hit();
for (int tower = 0; tower < kRHICfNtower; ++tower) {
    float totalE = 0.f;
    for (int plate = 0; plate < kRHICfNplate; ++plate)
        totalE += hit->getPlateEnergy(tower, plate);
    if (hit->isSaveDataArray())
        float l90 = hit->getL90(tower);
}
\endcode

\see StRHICfRawHit, StRHICfPoint, StRHICfCollection
*/
